      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>THE GERMAN PACIFIC SCHOOL OF SAN DIEGO (GPSSD) IS A LANGUAGE SCHOOL, OFFERING GERMAN CLASSES FOR CHILDREN AND ADULTS.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>GPSSD'S CORE PROGRAM ARE GERMAN LANGUAGE CLASSES FOR STUDENTS 3-18 YEARS OLD (3 HOURS/WEEK, 30 WEEKS/YEAR BETWEEN SEPTEMBER AND MAY). GPSSD IS TEACHING STUDENTS THE GERMAN LANGUAGE AND THE CULTURE OF THE GERMAN SPEAKING COUNTRIES AND PREPARING THE STUDENTS TO TAKE THE MAJOR GERMAN LANGUAGE EXAMS, WHICH ARE PROOF OF THE LANGUAGE PROFICIENCY WHEN APPLYING AT GERMAN UNIVERSITIES. GPSSD CONDUCTS 2 WEEKS OF SUMMER DAY CAMPS EACH YEAR, WHICH PROVIDES CHILDREN AGE 4-12 A FULL IMMERSION EXPERIENCE IN THE GERMAN LANGUAGE AND CULTURE. AS A COMMUNITY OUTREACH PROGRAM, GPSSD ALSO OFFERS WEEKLY ADULT CLASSES IN GERMAN LANGUAGE AND CULTURE.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
